MANUSKRIPT IMPORT FIXTURES — RIGHTS AND PROVENANCE
==================================================

Skribisto's own source code is licensed GPL-3.0-only (see COPYING at the repository
root). That licence governs the application. This note is about the fixture projects
in this directory and where their content comes from.


What these files are
--------------------

Manuskript projects, written by `generate.py` beside them, in the shape Manuskript's
own save code produces. They exist so this crate's tests can read a realistic
project tree: the modern folder layout, the single-file zip, and a zip written with
Windows path separators.

They are NOT files produced by Manuskript, and no file from the Manuskript project
is included here.


Why not a real Manuskript project
---------------------------------

Manuskript is free software under the GNU General Public License, version 3 or
later. Its shipped sample projects are part of that work, and FernTech does not hold
their copyright.

Everything in this repository has to be relicensable by FernTech: a commercial
edition links these crates as a path dependency, which is lawful only because
FernTech owns, or has been assigned under the CLA, every line here. Third-party
GPL material would break that, even material a test only reads. So the fixtures are
written rather than borrowed.

The importer itself was likewise written from Manuskript's file format as observed
in its source, not adapted from any existing reader of it.

Tests can still be run against genuine Manuskript projects, and should be. Point
SKRIBISTO_MANUSKRIPT_CORPUS at a Manuskript checkout and `tests/corpus.rs` reads
whatever it finds there. Nothing is copied into this tree by doing so.


The content inside the fixtures
-------------------------------

Chapter titles, synopses, characters and places are taken from the bundled example
`resources/examples/le_tour_du_monde_en_80_jours/`, whose own NOTICE covers it in
full. In short:

  Work:       LE TOUR DU MONDE EN QUATRE-VINGTS JOURS
  Author:     Jules Verne (8 February 1828 - 24 March 1905)
  Published:  1873, J. Hetzel et Cie, Paris
  Status:     public domain worldwide

The editorial text around it - the synopses, the story bible entries, the labels and
statuses - was written by the Skribisto project and is covered by the repository's
own licence.


Regenerating
------------

    python3 crates/manuskript_import/tests/fixtures/generate.py

Run from the repository root. The output is committed so a checkout can run the
tests without Python.
